Regional employment shock and "left-behind" energy regions
The phase-out of coal-fired power plants in Baden-Württemberg will lead to job losses among coal miners and power plant workers, as these facilities are a significant employer in the region. This could result in a regional employment shock, with potentially long-lasting impacts on the local economy. Additionally, residents in these regions may face increased energy costs due to the transition away from affordable coal-based power, exacerbating existing socio-economic inequalities.

